<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gamprin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gamprin is a small municipality in the Unterland of Liechtenstein, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eschnerberg">Eschnerberg</a>, comprising the villages of Gamprin and Bendern. On the church hill at Bendern the people of the Lordship of Schellenberg swore allegiance to Prince Hans-Adam I of Liechtenstein in 1699. The lordship later became the Unterland of the Principality of Liechtenstein.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gamprin.jpg" alt="Gamprin" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Markus K. Mayer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kirchh%C3%BCgel_Bendern.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
